    "history_en": "On Sunday 25 January 2026, American climber Alex Honnold climbed the outside of Taipei 101 with no rope and no safety gear, and reached the top of the spire. Netflix streamed it live as Skyscraper Live. The climb had been set for the day before and was pushed back one day because of the weather. Wikipedia records his time as 1 hour, 31 minutes and 43 seconds. He paused after the stacked middle section, nicknamed the bamboo boxes, to wave at onlookers. On top he took a selfie and said it was windy, then roped up for the first time to come down. The climb was authorized; he is the first person to climb the tower without a rope.",
